      "message": "While this change is simple, I suggest we still guard it with trunk-stable flag. We can use the `RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_TPU_ASSGINABLE_DEVICE` flag added in aosp/3236262, since ultimately this patch helps TPU assignment effort.\n\nIn order to guard this change behind the flag, you can do the following:\n\n1. Add new select statement under build/Android.bp (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/build/Android.bp;l\u003d21;drc\u003d812497f1bb2d60731763eb23758646ab2e8583c1). I suggest:\n\n```\nselect(release_flag(\"RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_TPU_ASSGINABLE_DEVICE\"), {\n        true: [\"tpu_assignable_device\"],\n        default: [],\n```\n\n2. Guard this code with `if cfg!(tpu_assignable_device)`.",
